{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1563050-viabillty-of-backporting-v6-mechanics-into-w5","id":1563050,"title":"Viabillty of Backporting V6 mechanics into W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-13T02:40:00-07:00","id":1563050,"title":"Viabillty of Backporting V6 mechanics into W5","content":"So Anyone actually think about back-porting some choice V6 mechanics into W5 to see how they work? Like this editions forsaken styled humanity bar would theoretically to the current (which isn't that impressive since the bar is set in hell and all...) and clan exclusive rage could be theoretically reworked into tribe exclusive Hauglosk which was intended to be made for the pre-regade version of W5. (an example from <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/c/jfsambrano/posts\" target=\"_blank\">J. F. Sambrano</a> patron is the Glass walkers going full techbro and decided to damming up a river to feed they AI servers so it could figure out a way to permanently seal away the wrym is a really good idea.)<br /> <br /> Like how much of other mechanics from V6 could conceivably improve W5 if any? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T04:24:20-07:00","id":1563052,"title":"","content":"Well, you could have Rage vs. Calm as a more volatile and temporary version of Mortal/Path vs. Monster. You're not permanently stuck at either one, obviously; going further toward Rage just gives you more points of Rage to use and makes it easier to frenzy (which the player will control), while going further toward Calm lets you step sideways easier and aids in recovering Essence and possibly in traversing the Astral Umbra if we can put in multiple Umbras in the core.<br /> <br /> I'd be leery of equating Rage or Essence with health, for obvious reasons, but I suppose you could do it. You'd probably want to wait to see how the playtest shakes out to make a call on that, though; as it is, we're still in pre-alpha, so &quot;V6&quot; is very much a hypothetical at this point rather than a realized thing close to being written in full.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T06:19:21-07:00","id":1563054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1563050-viabillty-of-backporting-v6-mechanics-into-w5?p=1563052#post1563052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be leery of equating Rage or Essence with health, for obvious reasons, but I suppose you could do it. You'd probably want to wait to see how the playtest shakes out to make a call on that, though; as it is, we're still in pre-alpha, so &quot;V6&quot; is very much a hypothetical at this point rather than a realized thing close to being written in full.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah using Rage + essence purly for health is kinda silly since the garou don't require magic to live unlike vampires and maybe mages. I think that rage only act as overshield for a conventional healthbar in warform and depleting it would knock the garou out of it.<br /> <br /> Also magic stat treated as health make mortal characters bit awkward to stat. Like how what stat determines health for a mundane hunter?<br /> <br /> Also V6 play test is going releases in about 5-6 months so I doubt the core system would change besides fleshing out the discipline and story path system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T09:56:42-07:00","id":1563063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1563050-viabillty-of-backporting-v6-mechanics-into-w5?p=1563054#post1563054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah using Rage + essence purly for health is kinda silly since the garou don't require magic to live unlike vampires and maybe mages. I think that rage only act as overshield for a conventional healthbar in warform and depleting it would knock the garou out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a bad idea, similar to the time restriction of W5. What's the use of a war form that you can get knocked out of doing the thing that it's made for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also magic stat treated as health make mortal characters bit awkward to stat. Like how what stat determines health for a mundane hunter? </div> </div> </div>Vitae is basically just layered onto health. So... health, without Vitae layered on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also V6 play test is going releases in about 5-6 months so I doubt the core system would change besides fleshing out the discipline and story path system. </div> </div> </div>This is a <i>pre</i>-alpha. They're throwing things at the wall to see what sticks in an even less finalized process than even a first edition WoD book from the early 90s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T17:56:25-07:00","id":1563077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1563050-viabillty-of-backporting-v6-mechanics-into-w5?p=1563063#post1563063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also a bad idea, similar to the time restriction of W5. What's the use of a war form that you can get knocked out of doing the thing that it's made for?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I know, though it's still lines up with Parawolf's brainwyrm (pun intended) on limiting warform the possible improvement theoretically it's less strict than W5 depending on how the numbers line up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vitae is basically just layered onto health. So... health, without Vitae layered on. </div> </div> </div>Yeah also I have an semi joke idea of tying heath to Wealth Resource in a theoretical H6 as the hunter's healthcare plan. With a major emphasis placed on SI characters since all the orgs facing budget cuts to justify them not being the man<sup>tm</sup>, Thus playable and running out of Wealth means they're burnt superiors for wasting resources.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}